# {{HOST_NAME}}

A SimpleModule host application, generated by `smpy create-host`.

## Quick start

```bash
# Install Python deps (framework + any modules listed in pyproject.toml)
uv sync

# Copy example env and adjust
cp .env.example .env

# First time only — initialize the migration history for the modules you
# picked. Inspect the generated file, then apply it.
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "initial schema"
alembic upgrade heads

# Run the API
python main.py
```

Dev UI + API together (when you have a `client_app/` alongside this file):

```bash
make dev    # if you ship a Makefile; otherwise run vite + uvicorn in two shells
```

Apps scaffolded by `smpy new` also ship Docker assets — `make docker-up`
builds `docker/host.Dockerfile` and runs the full stack from
`docker-compose.yml` (services match your `--db` choice), applying
migrations on container start.

## Adding a module

```bash
# 1) install the module package (e.g. from PyPI)
uv add simple_module_my_module
# or straight from a git repo (any host, private included):
smpy add git+https://github.com/you/your-module@v1.2.0

# 2) generate & apply the migration (new tables + any schema changes)
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add my-module"
alembic upgrade heads

# 3) restart the host — the module's routes, menu items, permissions,
#    feature flags, events, and health checks register automatically
```

## Disabling a module without uninstalling it

Set `SM_MODULES_ENABLED` to a JSON array of the modules you want loaded:

```
SM_MODULES_ENABLED=["Auth","Products"]
```

Unlisted modules stay installed (so the existing DB schema is untouched)
but don't contribute any routes, registries, or lifecycle work.

## Upgrading the framework

Modules declare `requires_framework` in their `Meta`. If a module can't
work with your installed `simple_module_core` version, the host refuses
to boot with `FrameworkVersionError` listing the offending modules.
Upgrade or pin as appropriate.


Your host owns its Alembic history: package upgrades do not import framework data
migrations. Run `uv run smpy doctor` after upgrading packages. For a reported
upgrade, prepare a revision against an explicit head in this host's graph:

```bash
uv run smpy migrations prepare mail.settings_namespace_v1 --head <your-host-head>
```

The CLI detects `alembic.ini` or `host/alembic.ini` (`--config` overrides it).
Preparation only writes a frozen, self-contained revision into this host's
`migrations/versions`; review it before running `alembic upgrade heads`.
`users.hashed_bearer_tokens_v1` deletes access/refresh credentials before changing
column types: stop all old workers first and expect clients to sign in again.
Fresh current baselines need neither recipe. Boot warns about unmoved mail keys
and refuses incompatible token storage outside development. Role seeding stays
an idempotent startup step. See the framework's scaffolded host upgrade guide.
